      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Secret Provider**\n\nOkay, I've decided to use AWS Secrets Manager and the `boto3` library. The focus is now on implementing the secret fetching logic within a Python script, named `fetch_db_secret.py`, to retrieve the database connection secret at runtime. I'm moving forward with AWS.\n\n\n**Defining Secret Fetching Logic**\n\nI've established the foundation for `fetch_db_secret.py`, opting for AWS Secrets Manager with `boto3`. My focus is now on crafting the secret fetching code within the Python script. I'll integrate `boto3` and explicitly reference AWS Secrets Manager to ensure the provider's identification. I plan to use placeholders for secret name and region, which I'll handle through environment variables later.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820820613,
          "start": 1789820818217
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9a253290014DrfkUj90w91S2",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9a24e44001EIm1BbwkquUqhx",
      "session_id": "ses_f465db1cdffetO7uO85DJVlTcq",
      "time_created": 1789820818217,
      "time_updated": 1789820820613
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "ySRldw0B48o6MUi9",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nimport os\nimport json\n\ndef get_secret(secret_name):\n    region_name = os.environ.get(\"AWS_REGION\", \"us-east-1\")\n\n    # Create a Secrets Manager client\n    session = boto3.session.Session()\n    client = session.client(\n        service_name='secretsmanager',\n        region_name=region_name\n    )\n\n    try:\n        get_secret_value_response = client.get_secret_value(\n            SecretId=secret_name\n        )\n    except Exception as e:\n        # For a list of exceptions thrown, see\n        # https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/apireference/API_GetSecretValue.html\n        raise e\n\n    # Decrypts secret using the associated KMS key.\n    # Depending on whether the secret is a string or binary, one of these fields will be populated.\n    if 'SecretString' in get_secret_value_response:\n        return json.loads(get_secret_value_response['SecretString'])\n    else:\n        return get_secret_value_response['SecretBinary']\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace \"YOUR_SECRET_NAME\" with the actual name of your secret in AWS Secrets Manager\n    secret = get_secret(os.environ.get(\"DB_SECRET_NAME\", \"YOUR_SECRET_NAME\"))\n    print(\"Fetched secret (partial view):\", {k: v for k, v in secret.items() if k not in [\"password\", \"token\"]}) # Print sensitive info partially\n",
            "filePath": "fetch_db_secret.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
