    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Secret Retrieval**\n\nOkay, I've decided on AWS Secrets Manager as the concrete secrets store. The next step is to nail down the specifics of fetching the API key using Python. I need to make sure the `fetch_api_key.py` file properly interfaces with AWS Secrets Manager, including authentication and error handling.\n\n\n**Implementing Secret Retrieval**\n\nI'm now implementing the `fetch_api_key.py` script. My focus is on integrating with AWS Secrets Manager via `boto3`. The code will specifically handle authentication and secret retrieval, using `boto3.client('secretsmanager')` and `get_secret_value` calls. I'm making sure to address error handling within this process.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820816152,
          "start": 1789820814054
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9a242e6001puAfd1nEEgeC4Y",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9a23d79001TMca81O77kcOar",
      "session_id": "ses_f465dc303ffe7aEfFghZZTLmak",
      "time_created": 1789820814054,
      "time_updated": 1789820816153
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "DCGhi0tP9Imbss3D",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nimport os\n\ndef get_secret(secret_name):\n    region_name = os.environ.get(\"AWS_REGION\", \"us-east-1\") # Replace with your desired AWS region\n\n    # Create a Secrets Manager client\n    client = boto3.client(\"secretsmanager\", region_name=region_name)\n\n    try:\n        get_secret_value_response = client.get_secret_value(\n            SecretId=secret_name\n        )\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error fetching secret: {e}\")\n        return None\n    else:\n        # Decrypts secret using the associated KMS key.\n        # Depending on whether the secret is a string or binary, one of these fields will be populated.\n        if \"SecretString\" in get_secret_value_response:\n            return get_secret_value_response[\"SecretString\"]\n        else:\n            return get_secret_value_response[\"SecretBinary\"]\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace \"your/secret/name\" with the actual name of your secret in AWS Secrets Manager\n    api_key = get_secret(\"your/secret/name\")\n    if api_key:\n        print(f\"Successfully fetched API Key (first 5 chars): {api_key[:5]}...\")\n    else:\n        print(\"Failed to fetch API Key.\")\n",
            "filePath": "fetch_api_key.py"
          },
